# Systems Programming in C (POSIX & Win32) Engineering Standards

This skill provides rigorous engineering standards, defensive programming idioms, and high-throughput architectural patterns for low-level systems development in **C (C11/C17/C23)** on Linux and Windows platforms.

---

## 1. Cross-Platform Abstractions & Defensive Memory Safety

### 1.1 Robust Pointer Arithmetic & Bounded Buffers
Never perform unchecked pointer increments. Always maintain pointer bounds:

```c
#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <string.h>

typedef struct {
    uint8_t *data;
    size_t size;
    size_t capacity;
} ByteBuffer;

static inline bool byte_buffer_write_bytes(
    ByteBuffer *buf, 
    const void *src, 
    size_t len) 
{
    if (!buf || !src || (buf->size + len > buf->capacity)) {
        return false; // Prevent buffer overrun
    }
    memcpy(buf->data + buf->size, src, len);
    buf->size += len;
    return true;
}

// Defensive pointer free macro
#define SAFE_FREE(ptr) do { \
    if ((ptr) != NULL) {    \
        free((void*)(ptr)); \
        (ptr) = NULL;       \
    }                       \
} while(0)
```

