## 5. Low-Level Sanitizers & Debugging Protocols

Always build test targets with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer:

```bash
# GCC / Clang Sanitizer Flags
gcc -O1 -g -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer -Wall -Wextra main.c -o app_sanitized

# MSVC AddressSanitizer Flags
cl /fsanitize=address /Zi /O1 main.c /link /DEBUG
```

### 5.1 Rules for Zero-Defect C Code
1. **Never ignore return values:** Always inspect error codes (`errno`, `HANDLE`, socket errors).
2. **Deterministic Cleanup:** Pair every initialization with an explicit destroy function (`_init` / `_destroy`).
3. **No magic sizes:** Derive sizes from types via `sizeof(*ptr)` instead of `sizeof(Type)`.
